FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after ferrion-passphrase-wipe.patch, ferrion-key-slots.patch and ferrion-mkfs-clear-ring.patch, for the Linux layer's sessions (LC3):
- `redoxfs --read-only IMAGE NAME` serves an image without writing to it: the image is opened for reading only, FileSystem::tx drops transactions instead of committing them (no access time is written), and the scheme answers every change (an open for writing, creating or truncating, unlink, write, chmod, chown, truncate, times, links, renames, a shared writable mapping, a received file) with EROFS.
- `redoxfs --memory MIB NAME` serves a new, empty file system held in memory, whose root directory has mode 1777, as /tmp has; it is gone when the daemon exits.

